          "turn_index": 2,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "How long before it starts working?",
          "answer": "The guidance I searched doesn't say how long a blue reliever inhaler takes to start working. I can't give you a time from memory.\n\nThe \"Asthma\" reference (General clinical reference, educational summary) does say that an attack that doesn't respond to reliever treatment, or that comes back within a few hours, needs prompt medical assessment. Don't wait it out if that happens.\n\nCall your local emergency number straight away if you have any of these:\n- Difficulty speaking in full sentences\n- Breathlessness while resting\n- Drowsiness or confusion\n- Blue lips or fingers\n- A chest that has gone quiet, with no wheeze, while you're struggling to breathe\n\nFor a timeline you can rely on, ask your doctor or asthma nurse how quickly your reliever should work and when to seek help if it doesn't. They can also write that into your personal action plan.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
